  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S.Saai Sakthi Minerals vs The Collector on 29 October, 2024 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.No.2915 In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated : 29.10.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr. Justice G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.No.29151 of 2019 and W.M.P.Nos.28945 and 28947 of 2019 M/ s. Saai Sakthi Minerals, Represented by its Proprietor, K.V.Srigandhi ... Petitione -Vs- 1. The Collector, Erode, Erode District. 2. The Tashildar, Erode, Erode District. 3. The Commissioner, Corporation of Erode, Erode. 4. The Assistant Commissioner, Zone -Iii, Corporation of Erode, Erode. ... Respondent Prayer : Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of Constitution of I praying for the issuance of a Writ of Certiorari, calling for all t on the file of the fourth respondent in Na.Ka.No.E1/2521/2017 dated 09.09.2019 and consequential order passed by the third respondent i Na.Ka.No.E1/2521/2019 dated 27.09.2019 and quash the same. Page 1 of 6 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.P.N For Petitioner : No appearance For R1 and R2 : Mr.V.Manoharan Additional Government Plea M/S.Saai Sakthi Minerals vs The Collector on 29 October, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/6581429/ 1 For R3 and R4 : Mr.M.Rajamathivanan Standing Counsel ORDER I L A N T H I R A I Y A N . J , m n h t t p s : / / w w w .",
    "facts": "3. The petitioner is in the business of processing the mineral water and supplying in the bottled containers in different quantities. While being so, the Government of Tamil Nadu passed an order in G.O.Ms.No.142, Public Works Department, dated 23.07.2014 for regulation of ground water extraction. Accordingly, the procedures have to be strictly complied with. While being so, the fourth respondent issued notice dated 09.09.2019 calling upon the petitioner to stop the water extraction from the bore well and supplying in the filled water can, within 24 hours. Thereafter, the third respondent issued an order to seal. Subsequently, the case of the petitioner is that the petitioner is not drawing water from the bore well for his mineral water business and he is purchasing water from out source. Thereafter, the petitioner was issued notice.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
